 him later  dexter learns that lila also has a  strange fixation as she is something of  a pyromaniac and sets her apartment on  fire to manipulate dexter eventually she  attempts to blackmail dexter into  getting back together with her all while  deborah learns that her real name is  lila west and she has a criminal history  eventually lila kills sergeant doakes an  innocent man in an effort to protect  dexter simply put dexter should have put  a stop to her dangerous actions long ago  sergeant doakes always had it out for  dexter he suspected the titular  character of being strange and likely  hiding something and he wasn't wrong in  fact he eventually learns the truth  about dexter morgan when dogs tries to  arrest dexter the serial killer  overpowers the sergeant and locks him in  a cell at a remote cabin at this point  dexter lays it all out on the table and  tells the sergeant that he is the bay  harbor butcher ultimately dexter commits  to evading law enforcement by framing  dokes as the serial killer dexter then  kills one of his targets in the cabin in  front of dokes after he witnesses the  shock of the police sergeant toward his  bold crimes he starts reflecting on his  past  that's when dexter realizes that harry  actually committed suicide because he  couldn't cope with his son's actions  despite teaching him the code and trying  to protect him the sergeant's shock  reflects what harry must have felt and  dexter considers doing the noble thing  which would be turning himself in  unfortunately for dogs lila finds the  remote cabin and burns it to the ground  with dogs and any evidence proving  dexter is a serial killer inside the fbi  then concludes that dokes is the bay  harbor butcher allowing dexter to walk  free while a moment of introspection  almost leads dexter to do the right  thing he still originally planned to  frame an innocent man for murder that's  low even by dexter's standards  while dexter's relationship with rita  begins with the sole purpose of  providing him with the camouflage he  needs to hide in plain sight it  eventually flourishes into some form of  legitimacy unfortunately however his  sociopathic nature leads to many  cringe-worthy decisions early in his  courtship with rita one egregious  example is when he plagiarizes his  marriage proposal from a killer who  romanticized a non-existent relationship  in her head my life was an unanswered  question  unanswered question  while this killer may have been far too  forthright with her delusions of love  dexter is the exact opposite therefore  he lifts her words and uses them as his  own when seeking rita's hand in marriage  once again for the benefits it affords  him  dexter had his fair share of ups and  downs but he always took pride in  following harry's code to the letter  however during the season 4 episode  slack tied the miami pd is hunting for a  killer after finding the arm of a model  inside the belly of an alligator this  turns dexter on to jonathan farrow a  photographer who takes twisted pictures  of female models who all appear tortured  or under duress  even i'm disturbed by this  dexter becomes intent on nabbing pharaoh  before the miami pd finds the evidence  that they need to make the arrest he  gets the suspect on his infamous kill  table the photographer adamantly insists  that he never killed anyone and that his  photographs are merely art dexter pulls  the trigger anyway and hacks the man to  death with a cleaver later he sees  detective batista taking pharaoh's  assistant into custody and charging him  with the murder of the women unbeknownst  to dexter uncovered surveillance footage  actually incriminated pharaoh's  assistant thus dexter was burdened with  the harsh reality that he killed an  innocent man  while dexter often lacks remorse he  demonstrates guilt over the idea that he  betrayed harry  season 4 of dexter is often considered  the best in the entire series and for  good reason john lithgow plays one of  the